 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "It may be that purer minds now expect\nThe gift of man's desire. Again,\nSee what with God, and with the divine,\nWhat is this little thing precisely?\nFor O thou in whom thy own soul resides,\nAnd who is best than mankind,\nHave ye no longer thought to decide\nWith Him the matter of the world? replied\nThe baby with the face of beauty,\n\"I do not ask thee for gold or statue,\nOr trees' store of jewels everywhere;\nFor life is a great pleasure",
